From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: pi-hrx-fabric <fabric@1bit.local>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 13:23:33 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] accel/amdxdna: don't invalidate an imported dma-buf BO at
 mmap time

amdxdna_insert_pages() marks an imported (dma-buf) BO's mapping invalid right after dma_buf_mmap()
returns. The invalidation puts the BO on client->bo_invalid_list, whose only drain path is
amdxdna_populate_range() -> mmget_not_zero() + hmm_range_fault() over the mapped vma. An imported BO's
vma is created by dma_buf_mmap() on the exporter's object, so it is not backed by the shmem pages
vm_insert_pages() installs for non-import BOs, and HMM cannot fault it in. The -EFAULT from
amdxdna_populate_range() is returned by the *next* aie2_cmd_submit() of the client, and because that
function drains bo_invalid_list client-wide before it looks at the job's own BOs, one imported BO fails
every later submission of that process - including the no-op admission transaction of a brand new
hardware context.

Measured on 0.18.0 (Linux 7.3.0-rc4, Strix Halo, NPU5/AIE2P): importing a GPU dma-buf and mapping it
succeeds, then kernel_queue_create() of a fresh context fails with -EFAULT (0x30000000E in the userspace
status) and the client stays poisoned for its lifetime. This is engine issue #812.

Importing a foreign dma-buf is only useful if the range can be executed on, so stop marking the
imported mapping invalid: population and migration of an imported range belong to its exporter, and the
driver has nothing to refault here. amdxdna_mark_mapp_invalid() loses its last caller and goes with it
(the driver builds with -Werror, which makes a dead static function a build failure), and the comment in
amdxdna_client_cleanup() that named it is corrected.

Provenance: this is the 2026-11-02 23:41 pair (ab885d8f, 412fdbc4) rebased onto the series this
directory carries. NOT INSTALLED anywhere, deliberately: loading it is the owner's call (#812), and the
runtime proof is the owner's run. Compile-proven here: pin + 0001..0005 + this + the next patch builds
to srcversion 336751493A77C50DE0B50F7, rc 0, no warnings.

Signed-off-by: bong-water-water-bong <bong-water-water-bong@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 drivers/accel/amdxdna/amdxdna_gem.c | 41 +++++++++--------------------------
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 31 deletions(-)

--- a/drivers/accel/amdxdna/amdxdna_gem.c
+++ b/drivers/accel/amdxdna/amdxdna_gem.c
@@ -496,36 +496,6 @@
 	amdxdna_gem_destroy_obj(abo);
 }
 
-static void amdxdna_mark_mapp_invalid(struct amdxdna_gem_obj *abo,
-				      struct vm_area_struct *vma)
-{
-	struct amdxdna_dev *xdna = to_xdna_dev(to_gobj(abo)->dev);
-	struct amdxdna_client *client;
-	struct amdxdna_umap *mapp;
-	int srcu_idx;
-
-	mutex_lock(&abo->lock);
-	client = abo->client;
-	if (client)
-		srcu_idx = srcu_read_lock(&client->hwctx_srcu);
-	mutex_unlock(&abo->lock);
-
-	down_write(&xdna->notifier_lock);
-	if (client && !abo->dying && list_empty(&abo->node))
-		list_add_tail(&abo->node, &client->bo_invalid_list);
-	abo->mem.map_invalid = true;
-	list_for_each_entry(mapp, &abo->mem.umap_list, node) {
-		if (compare_range(mapp, vma->vm_mm, vma->vm_start, vma->vm_end)) {
-			mapp->invalid = true;
-			break;
-		}
-	}
-	up_write(&xdna->notifier_lock);
-
-	if (client)
-		srcu_read_unlock(&client->hwctx_srcu, srcu_idx);
-}
-
 static int amdxdna_insert_pages(struct amdxdna_gem_obj *abo,
 				struct vm_area_struct *vma)
 {
@@ -549,7 +519,16 @@
 			return ret;
 		}
 
-		amdxdna_mark_mapp_invalid(abo, vma);
+		/*
+		 * Do not mark the mapping invalid. dma_buf_mmap() established the
+		 * mapping in the exporter's terms and the pages behind it are not
+		 * the shmem pages vm_insert_pages() would install below, so HMM
+		 * cannot refault them. Marking it invalid would put this BO on
+		 * client->bo_invalid_list, where amdxdna_populate_range() fails
+		 * with -EFAULT - and because that list is drained client-wide
+		 * before every submit, one imported BO would fail every later
+		 * submission of the process, not just the ones touching it.
+		 */
 
 		/* Drop the reference drm_gem_mmap_obj() acquired.*/
 		drm_gem_object_put(to_gobj(abo));
